#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:78
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`beans create \"<title>\"`. This is the AGENT's call. The workflow engine has no `create` op — its vocabulary is claim, note, resolve and archive, all of which act on an instance's existing bean."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:45
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent (this session)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Already exists?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the exact-title check before it (`todo-manager` §'Check before you create'): `beans list --json --search` followed by an exact comparison of titles, since `--search` is fuzzy. `no` (0 exact matches) creates the bean. `yes` (1 or more) does not create a second one — `beans create` mints a fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing — and asks whose the existing bean is."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered from the existing bean and its surroundings (`bean-coordination`). `someone else's` means a sibling is mid-flight on it: a claim naming a branch, a recent note, or an open PR. That bean is left alone and this process ends at Open_NotYours. `mine / unclaimed` claims it. A claim is branch-local, so check the bean's status on the store's tip and the open PRs naming it, not only the copy on your branch."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Check before you create (exact-title search)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Checks, creates and claims a bean it may hold. Open_Owner is the one branch this lane cannot finish itself: a bean that turns out to be someone else's goes to Lane_Sibling, and nothing on it is resolved, scrapped or edited from here."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Claim it (status: in-progress)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:108
#. Diagram label
msgid "Claimed — caller works it"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Create the bean (agent CLI, not an engine op)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "Durable work identified"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Idempotent. Claim BEFORE working, and note the branch, so a sibling session can see the item is taken rather than discovering it by collision. The only `claim` op in the corpus: every process that claims calls this process (`check:bean-calls`)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:88
#. Diagram label
msgid "Leave it alone (coordinate instead)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:116
#. Diagram label
msgid "mine / unclaimed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Never resolve, scrap or delete a bean another session or a human owns. Claiming is how two sessions avoid picking the same item; closing someone else's is how one of them loses work it had not finished reporting."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — caller stops"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sibling session or human (not yours to close)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "someone else's"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "STRICT. `beans create` is not idempotent: it mints a fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing, so re-entering a step duplicates the plan instead of no-op'ing. In the qou folio an unguarded re-run produced 14,688 duplicate beans — 92% of every open bean — which starved the idle-backlog policy of signal and collided with 15 real ids."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only task here with no `cat-harness.processes:bean` op: its whole job is to write nothing to a bean it does not own, ending at Open_NotYours so the caller stops rather than works."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The opening half of every bean's life: check before you create, find out whose it is, and claim it before any work starts — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. Called, never run on its own: the caller is the process about to do the work, and it calls this where the bean becomes its own. The caller's own gateway reads which end this reached. `Claimed` means the bean is in progress and the caller works it; `not yours` means a sibling holds it, nothing was written, and the caller stops. Process_BeanClose is the other half, called before each end the caller reaches after a claim."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:84
#. Diagram label
msgid "Whose bean?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
